"Hanoi, vibrations” is an art performance taking place at the Closing Gala of the Hanoi Festival of Creative Design 2026, held from 19:30 to 21:30 on Saturday, November 28, 2026, at the outdoor stage in front of Dong Xuan Market. Centered on the main concept "Kẻ Chợ under the Moonlight", the program is directed by General Director Nguyen Quoc Hoang Anh, featuring Nguyen Le (France) as Music Director and Guitarist, and People's Artist Tran Ly Ly as Lead Choreographer. It is presented by the French Institute in Vietnam - Hanoi and co-produced with Len Ngan and XPLUSX Studio.
Hanoi is remembered not only through images, but recognized by its sounds. It is a city that never stands still in memory; it vibrates through calls, footsteps, the bustle of market streets, singing voices, and human fates. The piece consists of six movements: Stillness, Opening, Ke Cho, Festival, Moon, and Echo, performed across three continuous acts: Awakening, Vibration, and Echo. It unfolds Hanoi’s collective resonance right from the space of Dong Xuan Market, where the sounds of everyday life become the raw material for creating a work of art.
In “Hanoi, vibrations”, Dong Xuan Market is not merely a venue, but the main character - embodying the distinct personality of Hanoi, Thăng Long - Kẻ Chợ. The core creative concept by Artistic Director Nguyen Le sparks inspiration and resonates seamlessly with the performing artists, guiding the audience through a rich spectrum of music,movement, and visual art: the Chèo melody "Con nhện giăng mùng" (The Spider weaves its web), the Xẩm ballad "Mục hạ vô nhân" (In my eyes, there is no one) re-imagined with blues and funk, the Quan họ song "Thỏa nỗi nhớ mong" (Satisfying the Longing) rearranged for a string section and band, call-and-response chants, festive drums, and the transcultural evolution of traditional Tuồng opera merging modern sounds in "The Offering", which bursts directly into artist Nguyên Lê's rock guitar rendition of "Voodoo Child"... All of these are the echoes of Hanoi past and present - a City experienced through human voices, rhythms, memories, and presence.
“Hanoi, vibrations” at the Closing Gala of the Hanoi Festival of Creative Design 2026 utilizes diverse artistic mediums to evoke the shared memories of Thang Long - Ke Cho: not merely visual memories of the past, but sounds that continue to be heard, interpreted, and renewed in contemporary life.
Creative Team: General Director: Nguyen Quoc Hoang Anh; Music Director & Guitarist: Nguyen Le (France); Head Choreographer: People's Artist Tran Ly Ly; Stage Director, Stage & Lighting Designer: Ha Nguyen Long (XPLUSX Studio)

Artists: Trung Bao: beatboxer; People’s Artist Thanh Hoai: Cheo; People’s Artist Hong Khiem: Tuong; Meritorious Artist Xuan Dieu: Dan Nhi; Phan Thuy: Dan Ty Ba (Thanh Am Xanh); Meritorious Artist Nguyen Quang Hung: Dan Bau; M.A., Meritorious Artist Le Van Mai: Dan Tranh; Nguyen Khanh: traditional percussion (Cheo Troupe, Vietnam National Traditional Theater); Jean-Sébastien Simonoviez : keyboard; and contemporary and breaking dancers.
